          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒲
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{W}
              \-type
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Martin-Löf82"}> Martin-Löf (1982), pp. 171
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Martin-Löf84"} (1984)
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/MartinLofIntuitionisticTypeTheory.pdf#page=49"} pp. 43
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            which is defined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} inductively
            in a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-founded+relation"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒲
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{W}
                ell-founded
            way based on a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            of “
            %em> c
            onstructors” and a type of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of “
            %em> a
            rities”. As such,
            = succeed "-types" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒲
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{W}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+types"} inductive types
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#WTypesInTypeTheory"} below
          %p
            The same terminology “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒲
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{W}
            \-type” is used &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "MoerdijkPalmgren00"}> Moerdijk &amp; Palmgren (2000)
            \&amp;rbrack; for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            in (suitable
            = succeed "-)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pre
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            which provide
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for the type-theoretic notion (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#WTypesInCategories"} further below
          %p
            Concretely, the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terms"} terms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            of a
