          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              If the type theory is
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identities
              have unique proofs and (dependent)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} extensional
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f=g
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)=g(x)
              for all
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} theoretic
              definition
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#WTypesInCategories"} below
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
              of familiar kinds of categories are all extensional in this sense.
            %p
              The main distinction from the naive categorical theory below is that the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheDisplayMap"} (1)
              must be assumed to be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/display+map"} display map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_f
              be defined.
            %p
              In the case of dependent polynomial functors, it seems that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              must also be a display map, in order to define
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_q
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjointness
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is not a display map. This more general version is what in type theory is called an
              = succeed ";" do
                %em indexed W-type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is a display map then one sometimes refers to
              %em non-uniform parameters
              instead of
              = succeed "." do
                %em indices
              %em uniform parameters
              are the kind discussed above where
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g f = h
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/red+herring+principle"} red herring principle
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/2011/04/18/whats-special-about-identity-types/"} this blog post
            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
              = succeed "-type" do
